Subject: Backport the Hadoop 3.5.0 module POM changes to Druid 37.0

Druid 37.0.0 builds its Hadoop-based extensions against Hadoop 3.3.6. Upstream moved to Hadoop 3.5.0 for Druid 38.0.0 in apache/druid PR 19273, commit https://github.com/apache/druid/commit/e738c9daa5ca8c660d7857cbcf7f5c6eed386d05, after Druid 37 had already dropped Hadoop ingestion. These are that commit's hunks for the extension POMs this package builds: hadoop-aws 3.5.0 brings the AWS SDK v2 bundle instead of the v1 bundle, so the deltalake and iceberg exclusions name the new artifact; Hadoop 3.5.0 adds jakarta.ws.rs-api, which conflicts with the Jersey 1 classes iceberg uses; and it no longer supplies joda-time transitively, so the extensions that compile against it declare it as provided.

Origin: DHI-internal (module POM hunks of apache/druid e738c9da, unchanged)
Forwarded: not-needed (upstream carries it from 38.0.0)
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/apache/druid b206640c830bc2c3bdc2867cfb317c902a0e1acb
Regenerate: `gh pr diff 19273 --repo apache/druid | git apply --include=extensions-contrib/druid-deltalake-extensions/pom.xml --include=extensions-contrib/druid-iceberg-extensions/pom.xml --include=extensions-contrib/druid-exact-count-bitmap/pom.xml --include=extensions-contrib/influx-extensions/pom.xml --include=extensions-contrib/kafka-emitter/pom.xml --include=extensions-contrib/momentsketch/pom.xml --include=extensions-contrib/thrift-extensions/pom.xml --include=extensions-core/avro-extensions/pom.xml`
Drop-When: never: the 37 leaf stays on Druid 37.x, which upstream does not move to Hadoop 3.5.0

